target:    tests/oracle/encoding_v1.py
gate:      composer test:fingerprint-v2-py
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    text must raise
rationale: Widens ONE language's accept-list past the pinned set (see encoding-spec.md, "Field encoding"). This is the failure the shared fixture was restructured to catch: before type_kinds and types_that_must_raise moved into golden-encoding-fixtures.json, adding a type to one side's list left every value assertion green while the two encoders had silently stopped implementing the same spec. Registered on the PYTHON side deliberately - it is the half whose gate is newest to CI. The mutation restores two of the four unauthorised types (text, char) that the first version of both encoders accepted.
---
diff --git a/tests/oracle/encoding_v1.py b/tests/oracle/encoding_v1.py
--- a/tests/oracle/encoding_v1.py
+++ b/tests/oracle/encoding_v1.py
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 # real schema does not declare — widening the accept-list widens the only safety property this
 # function has.
 _INT_TYPES = ("tinyint", "smallint", "int", "bigint")
-_STR_TYPES = ("varchar",)
+_STR_TYPES = ("varchar", "text", "char")
 
 
 def kind(declared_type):
 
